To generate the assert statement for the given comment, we need to express that for every index greater than the specified index and less than the previous size of the list minus one, the element at that index in the list after removal is either null if the old element at the next index was null, or it equals the old element at the next index.

Here is the assert statement in the required format:

<code>assert \forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size())-1; this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i+1)) == null ? null : \old(this.get(i+1)));</code>

This assert statement ensures that after removing the element at the specified index, each element at an index greater than the specified index and less than the previous size of the list minus one is correctly shifted and matches the old element at the next index.
